# Claim Jumper: the trigger needs an opponent to control MORE lands than you (CR 603.4: an intervening "if"). Bot1 plays a
# Plains on turn 1 and Bot2 an Island on turn 2: one land each, so casting it on turn 3 (the Moxen) triggers nothing, nothing
# is asked and nothing is shuffled. The opponent having fewer lands is the same refusal, and is covered by the same check.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Claim Jumper
Plains
Plains
Plains
Plains x6

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Claim Jumper.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Plains; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Mox Emerald; Claim Jumper
Bot1.Shuffles = 0
